WHAT: Removes InlineHint::Never from dispatch arm helper functions generated
by the Fe MIR lowering.

WHY: Each contract selector match arm generates a helper function for parameter
decoding. These were marked Never-inline, preventing Sonatina from merging
them into the dispatch function. Removing the hint allows inlining.

GAS IMPACT: None on any contract.

TEAM NOTES: This commit removed the inline hint but the Sonatina inliner
still didn't inline these functions — likely because they exceeded other
inlining thresholds or the cost model rejected them. The follow-up (step 21,
handler inlining) was needed to get actual gas improvement. This step laid
the groundwork.
